ry bookkeeping is consumed by campaign admission and proposal serialization. Thus application acknowledgement is authority-relevant. Delayed storage messages carry term/context to avoid using obsolete support, while committed decisions and application work are term-independent. Safe reads wait for current-term commitment and quorum context; pending precommit messages differ from the resettable readOnly map.',['b-authority','b-formation','b-membership','b-application','b-persistence','b-reads'],['f-applied','f-commit'],['s-election-entry','s-node-completion-contract','s-ready-completion','s-config-commit','s-storage-response','s-release-reads','s-read-acks']),core_gaps=[],open_details=['Applicability of early Advance before committed membership application and its effect on campaign eligibility.','Contract conflict on synchronous same-batch send/persist overlap.','Pending reads retained across reset and configuration-driven commit: narrower legal histories and permitted request loss need investigation.','Detailed storage failures, compaction concurrency, lease-clock bounds and special bootstrap histories remain outside this initial backbone.'],rationale='Representative formation and authority paths, their membership/persistence dependencies, old-work treatment, retries and consumption are sourced. Local completion-contract anomalies remain explicit rather than becoming unconditional Fact guarantees.'))\njson.dump(m,open('map.json','w'),indent=2)\nq=dict(question='When Node.Advance is used before application finishes, can raftLog.applied cause campaign admission to skip a committed configuration entry whose ApplyConfChange is still pending, and what caller obligation or alternative mechanism prevents stale-membership authority?',importance='If legally reachable, stale-membership campaigning could undermine eligibility and later quorum formation. This is potential consequence; neither a safety violation nor a legal execution history is established.',trigger_rationale='